.TH KANBAN 1 "2026-05-13" "rkb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rkb \- repository-level kanban board for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rkb build
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B rkb plan
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrkb\fR manages a kanban board stored in \fI.kanban-board\fR at the
repository root. It is designed for AI agents to break complex tasks
into tickets and track their progress.
.PP
The \fBbuild\fR subcommands mutate the board file. The \fBplan\fR
subcommands are read-only and output JSON to stdout.
.SH BUILD COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the board file if it does not exist. No-op if present.
.TP
.B add --title \fIstr\fR [options]
Add a new ticket to the backlog. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-description \fIstr\fR
Full description or acceptance criteria.
.TP
.B \-\-priority \fIn\fR
Priority level (1\(en5).
.TP
.B \-\-assignee \fIstr\fR
Name of the assigned agent.
.TP
.B \-\-tags \fIa,b,c\fR
Comma-separated list of tags.
.TP
.B \-\-blocked-by \fI1,2\fR
Comma-separated ticket IDs this ticket depends on.
.RE
.TP
.B move \fIid\fR \fIstatus\fR
Change a ticket\(cqs status. Warns if blocked tickets are not done.
.TP
.B edit \fIid\fR \fIfield\fR \fIvalue\fR
Modify a ticket field (e.g. title, assignee, priority).
.TP
.B rm \fIid\fR
Remove a ticket from the board.
.TP
.B archive-done
Move all tickets with status \fBdone\fR to \fBarchive\fR.
.SH PLAN COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [\-\-pretty]
List all tickets as JSON (or as a table with \-\-pretty).
.TP
.B show \fIid\fR [\-\-pretty]
Show a single ticket as JSON.
.TP
.B stats [\-\-pretty]
Show ticket counts per column, blocked count, and unassigned count.
.TP
.B export
Dump the raw board file to stdout.
.SH COLUMNS
backlog, ready, in-progress, QA, done, archive
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
Usage error or bad argument (missing --title, invalid status).
.TP
2
Board file error (not found, invalid JSON, I/O failure).
.TP
3
Ticket id not found.
.SH FILES
.I .kanban-board
JSON file in the repository root. Add to .gitignore.
.SH AUTHOR
rkb authors
